.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-trend 1  "trend " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-trend \- Show how health, findings and the rules or owners that moved most have changed across the snapshots `\-\-record` wrote
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx trend\fR [\fB\-\-last\fR] [\fB\-\-by\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-reporter\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-hyperlinks\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show how health, findings and the rules or owners that moved most have changed across the snapshots `\-\-record` wrote
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-last\fR \fI<N>\fR
Only the newest N snapshots
.TP
\fB\-\-by\fR \fI<BY>\fR [default: rule]
What to list the biggest movers of
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
rule
.IP \(bu 2
owner
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit one JSON object per series
.TP
\fB\-\-reporter\fR \fI<NAME[=PATH]>\fR
Where the output goes: `<name>` for stdout, `<name>=<path>` for a file; repeatable. The names are `terminal` and `json`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Do not open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
How a scan reports progress on stderr; `plain` prints a line every two seconds for a job log
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A bar on a terminal, nothing in CI or when stderr is redirected
.IP \(bu 2
bar: A bar whenever stderr is a terminal, CI included
.IP \(bu 2
plain: A line on stderr every two seconds and at each phase, for a job log
.IP \(bu 2
none: Nothing
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase output: `\-v` adds the configuration, the cache and every skipped file to the report; `\-vv` also prints stage timings and git commands on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-hyperlinks\fR \fI<HYPERLINKS>\fR [default: auto]
Render `file:line` in the report as a hyperlink that opens in an editor; `auto` enables it on terminals known to support hyperlinks
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal known to support them
.IP \(bu 2
always: Whenever the report is coloured
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .rqx/trend.ndjson]
The trend file `rqx scan \-\-record` appends to
